runExternalM2 -- run a Macaulay2 function in a new Macaulay2 process
********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        h=runExternalM2(fname,func,params)
  * Inputs:
      * fname, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, the name of the file that
        contains the function to run
      * func, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, the function to run.  Can
        also be a named *note Function: (Macaulay2Doc)Function, or *note
        Symbol: (Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,.
      * params, a *note thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,, the parameters for func,
        usually a *note Sequence: (Macaulay2Doc)Sequence,
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * M2Location => a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, default value
        null, the location of the M2 executable.  If null, then the absolute
        path of the first entry of *note commandLine:
        (Macaulay2Doc)commandLine, is used.
      * KeepStatistics => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,,
        default value false, whether to keep statistics on the resources used
        during execution
      * *note KeepFiles: runExternalM2_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmKeepFiles=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,
        => ..., default value null, indicate whether or not temporary files
        should be saved
      * *note KeepStatisticsCommand: KeepStatisticsCommand, => ..., default
        value FunctionClosure[../../../../../Macaulay2/packages/RunExternalM2.
        m2:677:27-710:1], an option that tells how to collect statistics
      * *note PreRunScript: PreRunScript, => ..., default value "true", a way
        to impose resource limits
  * Outputs:
      * h, a *note hash table: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable,, contains the output of
        func and other data

Description
===========

This function starts a short-lived new (``child'') Macaulay2 process, loads the
file fname, runs the function func with the parameters params, captures the
value returned by func, and stores it inside h in the original Macaulay2
process. Optionally, strict *note resource limits: resource limits, may be
imposed on the child process from within Macaulay2, or data may be collected
about the resources used by the child process.

Since the child is a new Macaulay2 process, it has no defined variables or
functions except those defined in fname. Hence, func and anything it needs
(e.g., ring definitions) must be defined in the file fname.

The hash table h stores the exit code of the created Macaulay2 process, the
return code of the created Macaulay2 process (see *note run: (Macaulay2Doc)run,
for details; this is usually 256 times the exit code, plus information about
any signals received by the child), the wall-clock time used (as opposed to the
CPU time), the name of the output file (unless it was deleted), the name of the
answer file (unless it was deleted), any statistics recorded about the resource
usage, and the value returned by the function func. If the child process
terminates abnormally, then usually the exit code is nonzero and the value
returned is *note null: (Macaulay2Doc)null,.

For example, we can write a few functions to a temporary file:

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : fn=temporaryFileName()|".m2"                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = /tmp/M2-45270-0/0.m2                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : fn<</// square = (x) -> (stderr<<"Running"<<endl; sleep(1); x^2);       |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|///<<endl;                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : fn<</// justexit = () -> ( exit(27); ); ///<<endl;                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : fn<</// spin = (x) -> (stderr<<"Spinning!!"<<endl; startTime:=cpuTime();|
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|while(cpuTime()-startTime<x) do for i to 10000000 do i; return(x););         |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|///<<endl;                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : fn<<flush;                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

and then call them:

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : h=runExternalM2(fn,"square",(4));                                       |
|Running (true && (/usr/local/bin/M2-binary  --stop --no-debug --silent  -q   |
|Finished running.                                                            |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|<"/tmp/M2-45270-0/1.m2" >"/tmp/M2-45270-0/1.out" 2>&1 ))                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : h                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o7 = HashTable{"answer file" => null}                                        |
|               "exit code" => 0                                              |
|               "output file" => null                                         |
|               "return code" => 0                                            |
|               "statistics" => null                                          |
|               "time used" => 5                                              |
|               value => 16                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o7 : HashTable                                                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : h#value===4^2                                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o8 = true                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : h#"exit code"===0                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o9 = true                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+



An abnormal program exit will have a nonzero exit code; also, the value will be
null, the output file should exist, but the answer file may not exist unless
the routine finished successfully.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : h=runExternalM2(fn,"justexit",());                                     |
|Running (true && (/usr/local/bin/M2-binary  --stop --no-debug --silent  -q   |
|Finished running.                                                            |
|RunExternalM2: expected answer file does not exist                           |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|<"/tmp/M2-45270-0/2.m2" >"/tmp/M2-45270-0/2.out" 2>&1 ))                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : h                                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o11 = HashTable{"answer file" => /tmp/M2-45270-0/2.ans}                      |
|                "exit code" => 27                                            |
|                "output file" => /tmp/M2-45270-0/2.out                       |
|                "return code" => 6912                                        |
|                "statistics" => null                                         |
|                "time used" => 4                                             |
|                value => null                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o11 : HashTable                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : fileExists(h#"output file")                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o12 = true                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i13 : fileExists(h#"answer file")                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o13 = false                                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Here, we use *note resource limits: resource limits, to limit the routine to 2
seconds of computational time, while the system is asked to use 10 seconds of
computational time:

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i14 : h=runExternalM2(fn,"spin",10,PreRunScript=>"ulimit -t 2");             |
|Running (ulimit -t 2 && (/usr/local/bin/M2-binary  --stop --no-debug --silent|
|Killed                                                                       |
|Finished running.                                                            |
|RunExternalM2: expected answer file does not exist                           |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|-q  <"/tmp/M2-45270-0/3.m2" >"/tmp/M2-45270-0/3.out" 2>&1 ))                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i15 : h                                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o15 = HashTable{"answer file" => /tmp/M2-45270-0/3.ans}                      |
|                "exit code" => 0                                             |
|                "output file" => /tmp/M2-45270-0/3.out                       |
|                "return code" => 9                                           |
|                "statistics" => null                                         |
|                "time used" => 2                                             |
|                value => null                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o15 : HashTable                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i16 : if h#"output file" =!= null and fileExists(h#"output file") then       |
|                                                                             |
|o16 =                                                                        |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|get(h#"output file")                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i17 : if h#"answer file" =!= null and fileExists(h#"answer file") then       |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|get(h#"answer file")                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+



We can get quite a lot of detail on the resources used with the *note
