We can handle most kinds of objects as return values, although *note
MutableMatrix: (Macaulay2Doc)MutableMatrix, does not work. Here, we use the
built-in *note identity: (Macaulay2Doc)identity, function:

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i20 : v=/// A complicated string^%&C@#CERQVASDFQ#BQBSDH"' ewrjwklsf///;      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i21 : (runExternalM2(fn,identity,v))#value===v                               |
|Running (true && (/usr/local/bin/M2-binary  --stop --no-debug --silent  -q   |
|Finished running.                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o21 = true                                                                   |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|<"/tmp/M2-45270-0/6.m2" >"/tmp/M2-45270-0/6.out" 2>&1 ))                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Some care is required, however:

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i22 : R=QQ[x,y];                                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i23 : v=coker random(R^2,R^{3:-1})                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o23 = cokernel | 9/2x+9/4y 7/9x+7/10y 7x+3/7y |                              |
|               | 3/4x+7/4y 7/10x+7/3y 6/7x+6y |                              |
|                                                                             |
|                             2                                               |
|o23 : R-module, quotient of R                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i24 : h=runExternalM2(fn,identity,v)                                         |
|Running (true && (/usr/local/bin/M2-binary  --stop --no-debug --silent  -q   |
|Finished running.                                                            |
|RunExternalM2: expected answer file does not exist                           |
|                                                                             |
|o24 = HashTable{"answer file" => /tmp/M2-45270-0/7.ans}                      |
|                "exit code" => 1                                             |
|                "output file" => /tmp/M2-45270-0/7.out                       |
|                "return code" => 256                                         |
|                "statistics" => null                                         |
|                "time used" => 3                                             |
|                value => null                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o24 : HashTable                                                              |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|<"/tmp/M2-45270-0/7.m2" >"/tmp/M2-45270-0/7.out" 2>&1 ))                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

To view the error message:

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i25 : get(h#"output file")                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o25 =                                                                        |
|      i1 : -- Script /tmp/M2-45270-0/7.m2 automatically generated by RunExter|
|           needsPackage("RunExternalM2",Configuration=>{"isChild"=>true});   |
|                                                                             |
|      i2 : load "/tmp/M2-45270-0/0.m2";                                      |
|                                                                             |
|      i3 : runExternalM2ReturnAnswer("/tmp/M2-45270-0/7.ans",identity (cokern|
|      stdio:4:74:(3):[2]: error: no method for binary operator ^ applied to o|
|                  R (of class Symbol)                                        |
|            ^     2 (of class ZZ)                                            |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|nalM2                                                                        |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|el(map(R^2,R^{3:{-1}},{{(9/2)*x+(9/4)*y, (7/9)*x+(7/10)*y, 7*x+(3/7)*y},     |
|bjects:                                                                      |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|{(3/4)*x+(7/4)*y, (7/10)*x+(7/3)*y, (6/7)*x+6*y}}))));                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Keep in mind that the object you are passing must make sense in the context of
the file containing your function! For instance, here we need to define the
ring:

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i26 : fn<<///R=QQ[x,y];///<<endl<<flush;                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i27 : (runExternalM2(fn,identity,v))#value===v                               |
|Running (true && (/usr/local/bin/M2-binary  --stop --no-debug --silent  -q   |
|Finished running.                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o27 = true                                                                   |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|<"/tmp/M2-45270-0/8.m2" >"/tmp/M2-45270-0/8.out" 2>&1 ))                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

This problem can be avoided by following some *note suggestions for using
RunExternalM2: suggestions for using RunExternalM2,.

The objects may unavoidably lose some internal references, though:

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
